From: XR1710G Community
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: allow RX decap offload for single-peer
 mesh links

mac80211 currently restricts RX decap offload to AP/STATION interfaces
via ieee80211_iftype_supports_hdr_offload(), so 802.11s mesh peers never
get IEEE80211_OFFLOAD_DECAP_ENABLED and never reach
drv_sta_set_decap_offload(). On MT7996 the firmware side is already
prepared: mt7996_mcu_sta_hdr_trans_tlv() sets the dedicated mesh flag in
the sta_rec_hdr_trans TLV for MESH_POINT vifs (upstream mt76 commit
88d1b002 "wifi: mt76: mt7996: enable mesh HW amsdu/de-amsdu support"),
but the translation stays disabled (dis_rx_hdr_tran=1) because mac80211
never asks for it.

Hardware decap strips the 802.11 header including the Mesh Control
field, so decapped frames bypass ieee80211_rx_mesh_data() and with it
mesh forwarding, TTL handling, proxy (AE) learning and RMC duplicate
suppression. Doing this unconditionally would break multi-hop and
multi-peer meshes, which is why the iftype gate exists.

Only enable it where those semantics are provably inert: a leaf mesh
point with at most one established peer (point-to-point backhaul). With
a single peer no mesh-layer forwarding can occur, and the local bridge
never forwards frames back out the ingress mesh interface, so no loop
can form. When the established peer count crosses the boundary, re-run
the offload evaluation from mesh deferred work (wiphy locked), which
tears down or sets up the per-peer decap state through the normal
fast-rx path.

TX is intentionally left on the software mesh path: enabling
IEEE80211_OFFLOAD_ENCAP_ENABLED for mesh would switch the netdev to the
802.3 xmit ops that have no mesh nexthop resolution.

Security model is unchanged: with decap offload the PN/replay check runs
in the WTBL hardware engine and A-MPDU reorder/duplicate handling runs
in the NPU, exactly as for AP/STA/WDS; no DUP_VALIDATED flag is faked
and no software check is skipped. Management frames (plink, HWMP) are
never translated by the hardware and keep the full software path.

Measured on Gemtek XR1710G (AN7581 + MT7996, 6GHz channel 37 EHT320,
single-hop 802.11s backhaul, Airoha NPU active): plain mesh was limited
to ~600-700 Mbps with 55-72% CPU on the receiving node, while the same
link in 4-address WDS mode (which gets decap offload) reached 1006 Mbps
with ~1-2% CPU.

Signed-off-by: XR1710G Community
---

--- a/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
@@ -2216,6 +2216,7 @@
 void ieee80211_recalc_txpower(struct ieee80211_link_data *link,
 			      bool update_bss);
 void ieee80211_recalc_offload(struct ieee80211_local *local);
+void ieee80211_mesh_recalc_rx_decap(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata);
 
 /* link handling */
 void ieee80211_link_setup(struct ieee80211_link_data *link);
--- a/net/mac80211/iface.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/iface.c
@@ -1067,6 +1067,27 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * RX decap offload makes the hardware strip the 802.11 header including
+ * the Mesh Control field, so decapped frames bypass ieee80211_rx_mesh_data()
+ * and with it mesh forwarding, TTL handling, proxy (AE) learning and RMC
+ * duplicate suppression.
+ *
+ * This is only safe for a leaf mesh point with at most one established
+ * peer (e.g. a point-to-point wireless backhaul): with a single peer no
+ * mesh-layer forwarding can take place, and the local bridge never
+ * forwards frames back out the mesh interface, so no loop can form.
+ * Meshes with more than one established peer must keep the full software
+ * mesh RX path.
+ */
+static bool ieee80211_mesh_rx_decap_allowed(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata)
+{
+	if (sdata->vif.type != NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
+		return false;
+
+	return atomic_read(&sdata->u.mesh.estab_plinks) <= 1;
+}
+
 static bool ieee80211_set_sdata_offload_flags(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_local *local = sdata->local;
@@ -1089,7 +1110,8 @@
 	}
 
 	if (ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_RX_DECAP_OFFLOAD) &&
-	    ieee80211_iftype_supports_hdr_offload(sdata->vif.type)) {
+	    (ieee80211_iftype_supports_hdr_offload(sdata->vif.type) ||
+	     ieee80211_mesh_rx_decap_allowed(sdata))) {
 		flags |= IEEE80211_OFFLOAD_DECAP_ENABLED;
 
 		if (local->virt_monitors &&
@@ -1152,6 +1174,14 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/* called from mesh deferred work when the established peer count changes */
+void ieee80211_mesh_recalc_rx_decap(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata)
+{
+	lockdep_assert_wiphy(sdata->local->hw.wiphy);
+
+	ieee80211_recalc_sdata_offload(sdata);
+}
+
 void ieee80211_recalc_offload(struct ieee80211_local *local)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata;
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh.c
@@ -1751,6 +1751,9 @@
 
 	if (test_and_clear_bit(MESH_WORK_MBSS_CHANGED, &ifmsh->wrkq_flags))
 		mesh_bss_info_changed(sdata);
+
+	if (test_and_clear_bit(MESH_WORK_RX_DECAP_RECALC, &ifmsh->wrkq_flags))
+		ieee80211_mesh_recalc_rx_decap(sdata);
 }
 
 
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh.h
@@ -54,12 +54,15 @@
  * @MESH_WORK_DRIFT_ADJUST: time to compensate for clock drift relative to other
  * mesh nodes
  * @MESH_WORK_MBSS_CHANGED: rebuild beacon and notify driver of BSS changes
+ * @MESH_WORK_RX_DECAP_RECALC: re-evaluate mesh RX decap offload after the
+ *	established peer count changed
  */
 enum mesh_deferred_task_flags {
 	MESH_WORK_HOUSEKEEPING,
 	MESH_WORK_ROOT,
 	MESH_WORK_DRIFT_ADJUST,
 	MESH_WORK_MBSS_CHANGED,
+	MESH_WORK_RX_DECAP_RECALC,
 };
 
 /**
@@ -393,6 +396,12 @@
 	return mesh_accept_plinks_update(sdata) | BSS_CHANGED_BEACON;
 }
 
+static inline void mesh_request_rx_decap_recalc(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata)
+{
+	set_bit(MESH_WORK_RX_DECAP_RECALC, &sdata->u.mesh.wrkq_flags);
+	wiphy_work_queue(sdata->local->hw.wiphy, &sdata->work);
+}
+
 static inline int mesh_plink_free_count(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata)
 {
 	return sdata->u.mesh.mshcfg.dot11MeshMaxPeerLinks -
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh_plink.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh_plink.c
@@ -375,8 +375,13 @@
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&sta->mesh->plink_lock);
 
-	if (sta->mesh->plink_state == NL80211_PLINK_ESTAB)
+	if (sta->mesh->plink_state == NL80211_PLINK_ESTAB) {
 		changed = mesh_plink_dec_estab_count(sdata);
+		/* the link may have dropped to a single established peer;
+		 * re-evaluate RX decap offload from deferred work
+		 */
+		mesh_request_rx_decap_recalc(sdata);
+	}
 	sta->mesh->plink_state = NL80211_PLINK_BLOCKED;
 
 	ieee80211_mps_sta_status_update(sta);
@@ -849,6 +854,10 @@
 	timer_delete(&sta->mesh->plink_timer);
 	sta->mesh->plink_state = NL80211_PLINK_ESTAB;
 	changed |= mesh_plink_inc_estab_count(sdata);
+	/* the new peer may have taken the link past the single-peer
+	 * boundary; re-evaluate RX decap offload from deferred work
+	 */
+	mesh_request_rx_decap_recalc(sdata);
 	changed |= mesh_set_ht_prot_mode(sdata);
 	changed |= mesh_set_short_slot_time(sdata);
 	mpl_dbg(sdata, "Mesh plink with %pM ESTABLISHED\n", sta->sta.addr);
